KWin: wl_output follows the refresh rate learned from presentation feedback (6.7.5 port of patches/kwin/0064, 2026-10-18)

For vitrine's 6.7.5 guest series (on its 1.27.1: Patch100-126, after kwin-nested-feedback-pairing and
kwin-nested-host-refresh). WaylandOutput::framePresented takes the host's refresh rate from presentation feedback
and sets it as the output's mode, but the logical output that wl_output reports copies its backend output only in
Workspace::updateOutputs(), on OutputBackend::outputsQueried. The backend's other mode changes emit it; this one did
not, so clients kept the rate the nested output started at: the highest host rate with kwin-nested-host-refresh.
On a host with a 165 Hz and a 240 Hz monitor, a guest full screen on the 165 Hz one told its clients 240 Hz all
session: mpv's display-resample fell to 48 frames a second, and Qt Quick's animation driver took 4.17 ms per
6.06 ms frame. Tested on 6.7.91 (findings/nested-wl-output-refresh-2026-10-18.md): wl_output 165.058 Hz, ideal
3/2 cadence. The same function on 6.7.5; this port only applies cleanly, it is not built or run here.

diff --git a/src/backends/wayland/wayland_output.cpp b/src/backends/wayland/wayland_output.cpp
index 3dade69..e04f934 100644
--- a/src/backends/wayland/wayland_output.cpp
+++ b/src/backends/wayland/wayland_output.cpp
@@ -399,6 +399,9 @@ void WaylandOutput::framePresented(struct wp_presentation_feedback *feedback, st
         next.currentMode = mode;
         setState(next);
         m_renderLoop->setRefreshRate(m_refreshRate);
+        // the logical output, and with it wl_output, follows only through the workspace's output
+        // update: without it clients kept the rate the output started at (60 Hz, or the guess)
+        Q_EMIT m_backend->outputsQueried();
     }
     const auto &frame = m_frames.front();
     if (auto t = frame.frameCallbackTime) {
